// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; The bounded run of the next-step law, host half (Refs #12884): one input event, one real call of
; queen::next_step::decide (through queen::next_step_run::run_decide), a check of the decision, at
; most one executor launch, an independent check of its artifact, then the next decision.
; A one-shot program: no daemon, no conductor, no cron, no network, no credentials, no shared
; service. Every file it writes is under target/next_step/ (gitignored scratch) in the cwd.
; The contract describes deduplication, fences, replay and the effect journal; the runtime
; behaviour is measured only by the journal of a run, not by this file.
; From the repo root:
;   NS_MODE=event NS_KIND=2 NS_SEQ=1 NS_EXEC=<absolute t27c> [NS_VERIFY=<absolute t27b>] next_step_main
;   NS_MODE=verify NS_VERIFY=<absolute t27b> next_step_main
;   NS_MODE=feed NS_FEED_DIR=target/next_step/<dir> [NS_LEASE=<pane>] next_step_main
; With NS_VERIFY set, an executed attempt goes straight on to the verifier and the next decision.
; NS_MODE=feed reads at most FEED_MAX_SNAPS pane-table snapshots <dir>/s1, s2, ... (t27os::pane_feed),
; keeps its own cursor in <dir>/cursor and journals each intended decision in <dir>/journal. It has no
; executor: nothing is launched, and target/next_step/run/ is neither read nor written.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module T27osNextStepMain;

